DROP table t1, t2;
In depend-ref join, PQ_single_queue may be generated by one PQ worker, which uses
its MEM_ROOT to allocate space. However, other workers can also utilize this
queue to fetch ctx. Once the worker that generated this queue has finished and
released its MEM_ROOT, other workers can read invalid node from queue; and thus
leading to the crash in BUG2022021400279.
CREATE TABLE `t1` (
`a` int NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,
`b` int DEFAULT NULL,
PRIMARY KEY (`a`)
) ENGINE=InnoDB AUTO_INCREMENT=65537 DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_0900_ai_ci
/*!50100 PARTITION BY HASH (`a`) PARTITIONS 8 */;
CREATE TABLE `t2` (
`c1` int DEFAULT NULL,
KEY `idx` (`c1`)
) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_0900_ai_ci;
